{"status":"completed","summary":"usb-storage is blocked on node1 both immediately and after reboot. The node restarted successfully and returned healthy with a changed boot identity.","actions_performed":["Created /etc/modprobe.d/usb-storage-blacklist.conf with blacklist and install-deny rules.","Ensured usb_storage was unloaded and verified an actual load attempt failed.","Rebuilt the initramfs so the rule applies during boot.","Rebooted node1 safely and verified recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Block usb-storage immediately","command_ids":["cmd-fae8a722e12545c2"],"summary":"modprobe resolved usb_storage to /bin/false; an actual load attempt failed and the module remained unloaded."},{"requirement":"Persist the block across reboot","command_ids":["cmd-d647e4ce9be644b7","cmd-6eb091b647534367","cmd-2d49ce2cb26146ea"],"summary":"The persistent rules were written, initramfs rebuilt, and after reboot both the filesystem and initramfs contained the rules. A post-reboot load attempt failed and usb_storage remained unloaded."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-71133e556c46468c","cmd-fec936c1698646dd","cmd-6355b6f395474539","cmd-2d49ce2cb26146ea"],"summary":"Baseline boot ID was b953e8ce-b303-4022-826c-3b5910ad1e9b with the system running; reboot scheduling was acknowledged; the recovered boot ID was 8c6f96a4-8c3d-41c5-b233-a5f328a792d9. The system returned running with its root filesystem mounted read-write and the blacklist effective."}]}
